WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:03.000
-Guys, today is Thursday.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.467
But I feel like
I was very busy today,

00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:08.100
and I need some time to write
out my thank-you notes.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
Is that okay?

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.901
I'd like to write out
some right now.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:16.467
James, do you have any
thank-you-note-writing music

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:17.434
for me there, please?

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.334
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.868
There he is. Classic.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:23.133
There he is.

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:25.467
He says -- He speaks with
his eyes, you know?

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:26.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.267
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:32.000
Thank you, Colorado Avalanche,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.033
for winning the Stanley Cup
in, well, a landslide.

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:37.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.234 --> 00:00:45.267
Thank you,
setting off firecrackers,

00:00:45.267 --> 00:00:47.234
for letting my uncle's fingers
celebrate

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.934
their independence
from his hand.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:03.000
"Was it worth it?"
"Nah. No, it wasn't."

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.634
Thank you, inflatable pool toys,

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.434
for sometimes not springing
a leak for a whole six minutes.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:12.367
Oh, that's interesting.
[ Applause ]

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:17.200
Repair kit.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:24.634
Thank you, fruit salad, for
being sangria that got sober.

00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:26.901
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.601
Not too shabby.
That's a good one.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.033
That's not bad.
That's not bad.

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:38.501
Thank you, NASA, for stopping
the sale of cockroaches

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.667
and moon dust
in illegal auctions.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:44.234
I guess now if you want to buy
cockroaches and dust,

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:45.734
you'll have to do it
the old-fashioned way --

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:47.267
by renting my first apartment.

00:01:47.267 --> 00:01:48.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.434
It wasn't that bad.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:59.467
Thank you, pistachios, for being
Pac-Mans that eat healthy.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.801
Thank you, lifeguard chairs,

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:12.234
for being tennis umpire chairs
on vacation.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:14.801
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my thank-you notes.

